{"n": 367, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "367.webp", "text": "30 23134\n\n3023 197\n\n23-2\n\nVersion with Shift Arm:\n\nLitt spring (1) out of tab (2) on the\ncase with a screwdriver and swing up.\nPull out bearing pin.\n\nInstallation:\nLubricate bearing pin lightly with\nMolykote Longlterm 2.\n\nModel M 3;\nUnscrew clamp for shift arm on trans-\nmission.\n\nUnscrew clutch siave cylinder on\ntransmission.\nPipe remains connected.\n\nVersion with DME:\n\nUnscrew heat shield.\n\nUnscrew bolts.\n\nPull out speed sender (2) and reference\nmark sender (3).\n\nImportant! — installation:\n\n‘Check Installed position.\n\nDon't mix up plugs.\n\nInstall speed sender (2) without ring In\nbore D and reference mark sender (3)\nwith ring (4) In bore B.\n\nEngine cannot be started if mixed up.\n\n(Check O-rings.\nInstall senders with Molykote Longterm\n2.\n\nimportant!\nFace end of OME senders must be\nwithout grease and dirt.\n\nSupport transmission.\n\nRemove cross member (1).\nLower transmission to front axie\ncarrier.\n\nInstallation:\nCenter transmission (see Group 26).\nTightening torque*.\n\nUnscrew transmission on engine.\nUnscrew Torx bolts with a Torx\nsocket\"*.\n\nRemove transmission toward rear.\n\nImportant! - Installation:\n\nWashers must be used with the Torx\nbolt version to avold Increasing the\nbreaking-loose torque.\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nimportant!\n\nCheck that dowel sleeves (1 and 2) are\nnot missing before Installation of the\ntransmission.\n\nAs applicable, transfer dowel sleeves\nfrom the transmission or use new\ndowel sleeves.\n\nCoat splines and guide pins lightly\nwith Microlube GL 261**.\n\nCheck oll level.\n\n* See Specifications\nSource of Supply: HWB", "words": [["30", 0.192, 0.281, 0.2031, 0.2902], ["23134", 0.2077, 0.281, 0.2359, 0.2889], ["3023", 0.187, 0.9749, 0.2127, 0.9828], ["197", 0.2177, 0.9749, 0.2319, 0.9828], ["23-2", 0.4592, 0.0257, 0.5086, 0.0501], ["Version", 0.2732, 0.0699, 0.314, 0.0818], ["with", 0.318, 0.0699, 0.3402, 0.0818],